<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dīreptĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		diripio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a plundering, pillaging</i> (rare, but good prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbs relicta direptioni et incendiis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 4, 1, 2</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">urbis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Verr. 2, 4, 52</span></i>
			; * <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C. 2, 12</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oppidi (with expugnatio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">profanorum sacrorumque,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 8, 3, 69</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sociorum (with vexatio),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Cat. 1, 7, 18</span></i>
			.—In plur., <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				4, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 44, 1 <i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>The stealing, rape</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aurei velleris,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 22, 8, 15</span></i>
			.</div>
